\f1\b\fs32 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Joan Mir\'f3\'92s 1971 
\f2\i \ul \strokec2 Le L\'e9zard aux plumes d'or
\f1\i0 \ulnone \strokec2  (The Lizard with Golden Feathers)
\f0\b0  is a masterpiece of the 
\f3\i \strokec2 livre d\'92artiste
\f0\i0 \strokec2  (artist's book) movement, where text, image, and physical book design fuse into a single, unbreakable artwork. Featured in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Museum of Fine Arts, Boston}} exhibition, 
\f3\i \strokec2 Picasso, Mir\'f3, Dal\'ed: Unbound
\f0\i0 \strokec2 , this exceptional object\'97bound in the publisher's vellum\'97was generously donated as a 
\f1\b Gift of Boris Fridman
\f0\b0 , a collector renowned for preserving landmark 20th-century avant-garde publications. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bonart.cat/en/n/47016/picasso-miro-and-dali-reinvent-the-book-as-a-work-of-art-at-the-mfa-in-boston"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 3}}]\
Visitors looking at this work can be told a compelling three-part story about it:\
