\f1\b\fs40 \cf0 1. The Artist as Poet: A Surreal Fable\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A Complete Vision:
\f0\b0  Unlike typical illustrated books where an artist interprets someone else's writing, Mir\'f3 authored both the surrealist poetic text and the visuals himself. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://choicecontemporary.com/collections/joan-miro-le-lezard-aux-plumes-dor?srsltid=AfmBOoqkQ77RqAWSO3c6TDHIHBVe54viQ3NYDqK05sLJDrbKROGzDX87"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.parkwestgallery.com/blog/joan-miro-broder-collection/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 3}}]\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Cosmic Lizard:
\f0\b0  The book unfolds like an abstract, mythic fable. A symbolic lizard journeys through an imaginative dreamscape of biomorphic forms, shooting stars, and celestial signs. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://choicecontemporary.com/collections/joan-miro-le-lezard-aux-plumes-dor?srsltid=AfmBOoqkQ77RqAWSO3c6TDHIHBVe54viQ3NYDqK05sLJDrbKROGzDX87"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 3}}]\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Visual Handwriting:
\f0\b0  Mir\'f3 did not use a standard printing typeface for the text. He wrote out the poems by hand directly onto the lithographic plates, ensuring his literary voice and painterly style were visually indistinguishable. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.parkwestgallery.com/blog/joan-miro-broder-collection/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

