\f1\b\fs40 \cf0 2. The Power of Print: Mourlot and Broder\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Technical Exploitation:
\f0\b0  Published by the visionary 
\f1\b Louis Broder
\f0\b0  and printed at the legendary Parisian workshop 
\f1\b Mourlot Fr\'e8res
\f0\b0 , the project pushed lithography to its absolute limits. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nationalgalleries.org/art-and-artists/113686"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}]\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Texture and Chemistry:
\f0\b0  Mir\'f3 combined aggressively splattered lithographic inks with soft, heavy crayon lines. He contrasted these raw textures against flat, blindingly vibrant fields of primary colors. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nationalgalleries.org/art-and-artists/113686"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}]\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 An Industrial Drama:
\f0\b0  The production was so complex that an entire earlier version from the 1960s had to be completely scrapped due to a technical flaw in the paper chemistry. The 1971 edition represents a triumphant, hard-fought victory of master printmaking. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs40 \cf0 3. "Unbounding" the Book\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Defying Expectations:
\f0\b0  As a central pillar of the 
\f3\i Picasso, Mir\'f3, Dal\'ed: Unbound
\f0\i0  exhibition, 
\f3\i Le L\'e9zard
\f0\i0  challenges what a book is allowed to be. It is not a container for information, but a sequence of 40 autonomous color lithographs designed to be experienced sequentially.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Living Margin:
\f0\b0  Rather than keeping art neatly framed on a gallery wall, this work forces visitors to look closely at how art lives in the margins, on textured sheets, and folded inside precious vellum. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.timeout.com/boston/things-to-do/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 3}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bonart.cat/en/n/47016/picasso-miro-and-dali-reinvent-the-book-as-a-work-of-art-at-the-mfa-in-boston"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 4}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 5}}]\
