\f1\b\fs40 The Secret Disaster: The Scrapped 1967 Version\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Original Effort:
\f0\b0  Joan Mir\'f3 actually completed a full set of stunning color lithographs for 
\f3\i Le L\'e9zard
\f0\i0  in November 1967.\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Chemical Flaw:
\f0\b0  After the entire first run was printed by Mourlot Fr\'e8res, publisher Louis Broder noticed a catastrophic defect. The paper chosen for the edition\'97a prestigious handmade parchment\'97reacted poorly with the unique chemical composition of Mourlot's heavy lithographic inks. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.schloss-ahlden.de/assets/images/auctions/catalogue-139.pdf"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 2}}]\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Degradation:
\f0\b0  Over time, the ink began to bleed unevenly, altering Mir\'f3's exacting vision of sharp lines and vibrant, un-muddled color fields. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 1}}]\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Total Scrap:
\f0\b0  Refusing to compromise on quality, Broder and Mir\'f3 made the agonizing decision to reject and physically destroy the entire completed 1967 edition, rendering years of painstaking work completely obsolete.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs40 \cf0 The 1971 Triumph: Mourlot and Broder's Redemption\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0
\fs32 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Starting Over:
\f0\b0  To salvage the project, Mir\'f3 had to completely recreate his vision on entirely new lithographic stones and plates.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Flawless Paper Chemistry:
\f0\b0  Mourlot Fr\'e8res spent years reformulating their technical approach, eventually settling on flawlessly manufactured, watermarked 
\f1\b B.F.K. Rives paper
\f0\b0  (and a highly limited run on pristine vellum/parchment) that could permanently hold the saturation of Mir\'f3\'92s primary colors without chemical degradation.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Final Masterpiece:
\f0\b0  Released finally in 1971, the book emerged not just as an art piece, but as a legendary symbol of printmaking resilience. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.schloss-ahlden.de/assets/images/auctions/catalogue-139.pdf"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mfa.org/exhibition/picasso-miro-dali-unbound"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/search?q=product&prds=pvt:hg,productid:12440717705667319651&ibp=oshop"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 3}}]\
